cel reports can be automated using Power Query (built into Excel, no coding needed), VBA macros, or Python scripts — depending on complexity. The right choice depends on what your data looks like and how technical your team is. For most UK SMEs, ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Power Query handles 80% of cases"}]," and requires no coding at all."]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"17px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.85","marginBottom":"32px"},"children":"The average UK finance team spends around 8 hours per week on manual spreadsheet work. That is one full working day, every week, doing something a computer could do in seconds. Over a year, that is roughly 400 hours — or about £15,000 in salary time, depending on who is doing it."}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"17px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.85","marginBottom":"48px"},"children":"The frustrating part is that most of this is genuinely automatable. The export-to-report cycle — pulling data from your accounting software, pasting it into Excel, adjusting formulas, formatting it, emailing it out — does not need a human. It needs a well-built system. Here is how to build one."}],["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"clamp(1.4rem, 2.5vw, 1.9rem)","marginBottom":"20px","letterSpacing":"-0.02em"},"children":"Why most Excel reports are still manual"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"17px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.85","marginBottom":"24px"},"children":"Excel was designed in 1987 as a tool for small amounts of data. It was never meant to be the backbone of a business reporting system. But because it is familiar and flexible, it ends up being used for everything — and over time, reports get built manually, month after month, because that is how it has always been done."}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"17px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.85","marginBottom":"48px"},"children":"The result is what finance teams call Excel hell: version conflicts, broken formulas, reports that only one person knows how to run, and decisions made on data that is already three weeks old. Sound familiar?"}],["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"clamp(1.4rem, 2.5vw, 1.9rem)","marginBottom":"20px","letterSpacing":"-0.02em"},"children":"The four main ways to automate Excel reports"}],[["$","div","0",{"style":{"padding":"28px","background":"var(--bg-2)","borderRadius":"var(--radius-lg)","border":"1px solid var(--border)","marginBottom":"24px","borderTop":"3px solid var(--amber)"},"children":[["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","justifyContent":"space-between","alignItems":"flex-start","marginBottom":"16px","flexWrap":"wrap","gap":"8px"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1.15rem","margin":0},"children":"1. Power Query — the no-code option"}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"500","color":"var(--amber)","background":"var(--amber)18","padding":"3px 10px","borderRadius":"100px","border":"1px solid var(--amber)40"},"children":"Best for most businesses"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"15px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.75","marginBottom":"12px"},"children":"Power Query is built into Excel and has been available since 2016. Most businesses have never heard of it. It connects directly to your data sources — other Excel files, CSV exports, Xero, SharePoint, SQL databases, and hundreds more — and transforms that data automatically every time you refresh."}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"15px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.75","marginBottom":"20px"},"children":"You set it up once by recording what you want it to do: pull the data, clean it, reshape it, combine it. After that, refreshing the report takes one click. No formulas to break, no copy-paste, no formatting from scratch."}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"grid","gridTemplateColumns":"1fr 1fr","gap":"16px"},"children":[["$","div",null,{"style":{"padding":"14px","background":"rgba(34,197,94,0.06)","borderRadius":"8px","border":"1px solid rgba(34,197,94,0.15)"},"children":[["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"600","color":"#16a34a","marginBottom":"6px"},"children":"WORKS WELL FOR"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"13px","color":"var(--ink-3)","margin":0,"lineHeight":"1.6"},"children":"No coding required, built into Excel, handles most SME reporting needs, easy for non-technical staff to refresh"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"padding":"14px","background":"rgba(239,68,68,0.06)","borderRadius":"8px","border":"1px solid rgba(239,68,68,0.15)"},"children":[["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"600","color":"#dc2626","marginBottom":"6px"},"children":"WATCH OUT FOR"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"13px","color":"var(--ink-3)","margin":0,"lineHeight":"1.6"},"children":"Requires initial setup time, limited for very complex logic, refresh is manual unless combined with Power Automate"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"style":{"padding":"28px","background":"var(--bg-2)","borderRadius":"var(--radius-lg)","border":"1px solid var(--border)","marginBottom":"24px","borderTop":"3px solid #6b7280"},"children":[["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","justifyContent":"space-between","alignItems":"flex-start","marginBottom":"16px","flexWrap":"wrap","gap":"8px"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1.15rem","margin":0},"children":"2. VBA Macros — the automation workhorse"}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"500","color":"#6b7280","background":"#6b728018","padding":"3px 10px","borderRadius":"100px","border":"1px solid #6b728040"},"children":"Best for repetitive complex tasks"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"15px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.75","marginBottom":"12px"},"children":"VBA (Visual Basic for Applications) is Excel's built-in scripting language. A VBA macro can automate almost anything you can do manually in Excel — formatting, calculations, emailing reports, saving PDFs, combining files — and run it all with one button press or on a schedule."}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"15px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.75","marginBottom":"20px"},"children":"You do not need to write VBA from scratch. A consultant can build the macro once, and your team just runs it. The code lives inside the Excel file itself, so there is nothing extra to install."}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"grid","gridTemplateColumns":"1fr 1fr","gap":"16px"},"children":[["$","div",null,{"style":{"padding":"14px","background":"rgba(34,197,94,0.06)","borderRadius":"8px","border":"1px solid rgba(34,197,94,0.15)"},"children":[["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"600","color":"#16a34a","marginBottom":"6px"},"children":"WORKS WELL FOR"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"13px","color":"var(--ink-3)","margin":0,"lineHeight":"1.6"},"children":"Extremely powerful, can automate the entire reporting process end-to-end, runs inside Excel with no additional software"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"padding":"14px","background":"rgba(239,68,68,0.06)","borderRadius":"8px","border":"1px solid rgba(239,68,68,0.15)"},"children":[["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"600","color":"#dc2626","marginBottom":"6px"},"children":"WATCH OUT FOR"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"13px","color":"var(--ink-3)","margin":0,"lineHeight":"1.6"},"children":"Requires someone to write it initially, some IT departments block macros for security reasons, harder to maintain if the original developer leaves"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div","2",{"style":{"padding":"28px","background":"var(--bg-2)","borderRadius":"var(--radius-lg)","border":"1px solid var(--border)","marginBottom":"24px","borderTop":"3px solid #3b82f6"},"children":[["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","justifyContent":"space-between","alignItems":"flex-start","marginBottom":"16px","flexWrap":"wrap","gap":"8px"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1.15rem","margin":0},"children":"3. Python — for serious data volumes"}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"500","color":"#3b82f6","background":"#3b82f618","padding":"3px 10px","borderRadius":"100px","border":"1px solid #3b82f640"},"children":"Best for large or complex data"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"15px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.75","marginBottom":"12px"},"children":"Python is the tool of choice when your data is too large for Excel to handle comfortably, comes from multiple systems that do not connect easily, or requires complex processing logic. A Python script can pull data from APIs, databases, and files, process thousands of rows in seconds, and output a clean Excel report automatically."}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"15px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.75","marginBottom":"20px"},"children":"Python automation typically runs on a schedule — daily, weekly, or monthly — so the report is simply there when you need it, with no human involvement at all."}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"grid","gridTemplateColumns":"1fr 1fr","gap":"16px"},"children":[["$","div",null,{"style":{"padding":"14px","background":"rgba(34,197,94,0.06)","borderRadius":"8px","border":"1px solid rgba(34,197,94,0.15)"},"children":[["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"600","color":"#16a34a","marginBottom":"6px"},"children":"WORKS WELL FOR"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"13px","color":"var(--ink-3)","margin":0,"lineHeight":"1.6"},"children":"Handles any data volume, connects to virtually any source, can run fully automatically on a schedule"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"padding":"14px","background":"rgba(239,68,68,0.06)","borderRadius":"8px","border":"1px solid rgba(239,68,68,0.15)"},"children":[["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"600","color":"#dc2626","marginBottom":"6px"},"children":"WATCH OUT FOR"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"13px","color":"var(--ink-3)","margin":0,"lineHeight":"1.6"},"children":"Requires a dev