tyle":{"fontSize":"17px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.85","marginBottom":"48px"},"children":"Automated reporting solves this completely. When the process is built into a system rather than a person, it runs regardless of who is in the office. The report arrives on Monday morning whether or not the person who used to build it is still with the company."}],["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"clamp(1.4rem, 2.5vw, 1.9rem)","marginBottom":"20px","letterSpacing":"-0.02em"},"children":"What does Excel automation actually cost?"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"17px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.85","marginBottom":"24px"},"children":"At Lexalytic, a typical Excel automation project costs between £495 and £1,500 depending on complexity. Most projects are delivered within 3 to 7 days."}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"17px","color":"var(--ink-2)","lineHeight":"1.85","marginBottom":"48px"},"children":"Compare that to the cost of manual reporting: if one person spends 8 hours a week on spreadsheets at a salary of £35,000 a year, that is roughly £6,700 per year in salary time. A £750 automation project pays for itself in about six weeks — and keeps paying back every week after that."}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"padding":"36px","background":"var(--bg-dark)","borderRadius":"var(--radius-lg)","textAlign":"center","marginBottom":"48px"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"color":"var(--white)","marginBottom":"12px","fontSize":"1.4rem"},"children":"Want your Excel reports to run themselves?"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"color":"rgba(255,255,255,0.5)","marginBottom":"28px","fontSize":"15px","lineHeight":"1.7"},"children":"Book a free 30-minute scoping call. Show us your current process and we will tell you exactly what can be automated, how long it will take, and what it will cost — before you commit to anything."}],["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/#contact","className":"btn-amber","style":{"fontSize":"15px","padding":"14px 32px"},"children":"Book a free scopi